## Rules

1. **One Checklist Step at a time** — never work on multiple in parallel.
2. **One commit per Checklist Step** — after Tester PASS, and in that **same commit tick the step's `## EXECUTION STATE` box** (`- [ ]` → `- [x]`) so the ticket's progress index stays accurate — this keeps V1 tickets consistent and lets the V2 Conductor detect completion / resume correctly. If `git status` shows nothing to commit although Refactorer reported "Step N done", that is a failure (see On Failure). Do not batch commits.
3. **Subagents by exact name** — `architect`, `refactorer`, `verifier`, `tester` so Cursor routes correctly. Subagent definitions: `.cursor/agents/`. The `bugbot` subagent is the one exception: it is not delegated by name but launched by the Orchestrator through the `/review-bugbot` skill at the Local Bugbot Review stage.
4. **One version bump per PR** — the Finalize step bumps `app/system/config.php` exactly once per Roadmap Step / PR. Subsequent mini-loop fix commits (Local Bugbot review mini-loop, Final Test mini-loop) on the same PR/branch **must not** trigger another `chore(release): bump version to ...` commit. The CHANGELOG-NEW.md section for the already-bumped version is amended in place to include the mini-loop changes; the ROADMAP header pointer stays on the same version. Rationale: the PR is one logical release unit. Re-bumping mid-review wastes commits, confuses readers of `git log`, and creates a fictitious version that was never tagged.
5. **Ticket is a durable artifact** — immediately after the Architect writes `migration-docs/tickets/active/{task-slug}_plan.md`, the Orchestrator commits it (`docs(plan): add ticket for <task-slug>`) before the Refactorer loop. Tickets are tracked and land in the PR; they are **never** left untracked or gitignored.

## Local Bugbot Review (after all Checklist Steps committed, before Early Push)

Orchestrator (no subagent in the usual sense — it runs the `/review-bugbot` skill, which launches the read-only `bugbot` subagent):

1. **Run** — invoke `/review-bugbot` on `branch changes` (the full branch diff vs. the merge-base with the base branch). The `bugbot` subagent computes the diff itself; do **not** push or open a PR first, and do not compute the diff manually. See `.cursor/skills-cursor/review-bugbot/SKILL.md` for the exact prompt shape and `.cursor/BUGBOT.md` for the project-specific review criteria.
2. **Decide** — no findings → proceed to Early Push. Findings → mini-loop: pass the findings verbatim to the **refactorer**, then **verifier** → **tester** → commit, then re-run `/review-bugbot`. Repeat until clean.

Run Bugbot **once per PR** at this stage — **not** per Checklist Step. The Verifier already performs static review on every step; a per-step Bugbot run would duplicate that and waste tokens. This stage replaces the old remote Bugbot quick-peek entirely.

**Why local, before the push:** `/review-bugbot` stores the patch ID of the reviewed diff. When the Early Push opens a PR with the same diff, the remote Cursor Bugbot recognizes that patch ID and **skips** its PR review — no double review, no waiting on the ~15-min remote run, no GraphQL polling. The effort level (`Default`/`High`) is a global Bugbot dashboard setting and cannot be selected per invocation; do not attempt to switch modes from the workflow.

## Early Push (after Local Bugbot Review)

Orchestrator (no subagent):

1. **Push** — `git push -u origin HEAD` from the feature branch.
2. **PR creation** — `gh pr create` with the `<!-- metadata -->` block (labels, milestone, `closes`). Use the GitHub Issue number from the invocation (`GitHub Issue: #XXX`). Include `Closes #XXX` in PR body AND in the metadata `closes:` field. See `push.mdc` § PR Metadata + `github-labels.mdc`.

This early push triggers CI (PHP Quality workflow). The Final Test step waits on those CI checks. The remote Cursor Bugbot skips its review thanks to the patch-ID sync from the Local Bugbot Review above; any findings were already handled locally, so there is no separate Bugbot peek step.

## Final Test (after Early Push)

Sequential: (a) the **Orchestrator** waits on CI itself — `gh run watch` on the PHP Quality jobs (a watch, not a test, so no subagent) — until green; (b) **then** it delegates the 3 Playwright E2E specs to the **tester** ("final E2E run"), so the expensive E2E run only happens on code that already passes CI. See `tester.md` § End-of-ticket tests for the E2E commands. On FAIL (either side) → Refactorer → Verifier → Tester mini-loop, commit, push, re-run.

## Finalize (after Final Test PASS)

Orchestrator (no subagent) executes the relevant items of **push.mdc**:

1. **Branch documentation** — Create `migration-docs/branches/phase-<N>/{task-name}.md` (where `<N>` is the major phase number of the Roadmap Step — e.g. Step 2.1.8 → `phase-2/`; create the `phase-<N>/` folder if it does not yet exist) documenting:
   - All changes made (files, what changed, why)
   - Breaking changes for extensions (if any)
   - Test results summary (CI run reference + local E2E results)
   - Referenced **Roadmap Step X.Y** and GitHub Issue
   - PR number (now known from Early Push)
     Use existing files in the matching `migration-docs/branches/phase-<N>/` folder as reference for format/style.
2. **Version bump** — `.cursor/skills/version-bump/SKILL.md`
3. **CHANGELOG-NEW.md** — group all commits from this Roadmap Step
4. **ROADMAP update** — `.cursor/ROADMAP.md` (Header pointer, this step's row Status `⏳` → `✅`, Audit `⏳` → `🛡️`, **PR `-` → `#YYY`**, plus Phase 1 audit closures per `push.mdc`)
5. **Archive ticket** — `git mv migration-docs/tickets/active/{task-slug}_plan.md migration-docs/tickets/done/` (the step is complete; the ticket leaves the `active/` namespace). Include this in the finalize commits.
6. **Push** (second push) — updates the PR with the finalize commits.
7. **Do NOT merge** — user reviews and merges.

## On Failure (CRITICAL — do not self-fix)

The Orchestrator NEVER fixes code, reads files to understand errors, or runs tests to verify fixes. On ANY failure:

| Failure                                        | Action                                                                                                                                       |
| ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Refactorer reported done but tree clean**    | Re-delegate to **refactorer**: "Ticket: …, Checklist Step N. No changes detected on disk. Re-execute and emit changed files."                |
| **Verifier FAIL**                              | Pass feedback to **refactorer**: "Ticket: …, Checklist Step N. Verifier feedback: [paste FAIL output verbatim]. Delegate to **refactorer**." |
| **Tester FAIL**                                | Pass feedback to **refactorer**: "Ticket: …, Checklist Step N. Tester feedback: [paste FAIL output verbatim]. Delegate to **refactorer**."   |
| **Refactorer cannot fix** (architecture issue) | Escalate to **architect**: "Ticket: …, Checklist Step N. Issue: [one line]. Delegate to **architect**."                                      |

After any fix: restart the loop from **verifier** (not from commit), then **tester**, then commit. Never amend commits yourself; let the refactorer produce clean changes, then commit normally.
